add('# Moker health check — 25 September 2026\n')
add('**Completed: 2,000 four-orbit basic tournaments and 2,000 standard riichi games, plus 1,800 sensitivity/control runs (5,800 total runs).** Four identical bots using the default policy per table, deterministic seeds, rules v5 captured at the start of the run. This is a bot-play balance study, not a prediction of human or optimal play.\n')
add('## Assessment\n')
add('**Accounting passed; the balance verdict is sensitive to bot settings.** The large, four-sample batch suppresses voluntary all-ins by construction. Higher-sample bots create much more elimination and borrowing pressure. Treat the default-setting results below as the more relevant stress check, with wider uncertainty from the smaller sample. Fix or calibrate the bot limitations before using simulation alone to approve the chip economy or nerf special cards.\n')
table(['Equity samples','Runs per mode','Basic elimination / player-orbit','Basic all-in hands','Riichi loans / game','Riichi negative final scores'],[[samples,n(s[f'basic-s{samples}-c200']['runs']),pct(s[f'basic-s{samples}-c200']['eliminations']['clusterRate']['rate']),pct(s[f'basic-s{samples}-c200']['allInHandRate']),f2(s[f'riichi-s{samples}-c200']['loans']['loansPerGame']['mean']),pct(s[f'riichi-s{samples}-c200']['negativeScores']/(4*s[f'riichi-s{samples}-c200']['runs']))] for samples in [4,12,24]])
table(['Samples','Basic hands reaching Street 4','Riichi hands reaching Street 4','Riichi all-in hands'],[[samples,pct(s[f'basic-s{samples}-c200']['endingStreets'].get('4',0)/s[f'basic-s{samples}-c200']['hands']),pct(s[f'riichi-s{samples}-c200']['endingStreets'].get('4',0)/s[f'riichi-s{samples}-c200']['hands']),pct(s[f'riichi-s{samples}-c200']['allInHandRate'])] for samples in [4,12,24]])
add('The 24-sample setting is the captured app default. Changing sample count also changes confidence shrinkage and which aggressive actions the bot considers; this is more than simply reducing measurement noise. Matched-seed comparisons below confirm the effect.\n')
add('## Scope and reliability\n')
add('Basic tournaments use four separate dealer orbits, with fresh 200/300/400/500-chip stacks and 5/10/15/20 antes. Eliminated players return in the next orbit; final scores sum all four game scores. Standard riichi games use one four-seat dealer orbit, 200 starting chips, three sticks each, and automatic 200-chip loans when needed to ante, penalized by 250 at settlement.\n')
add('The main batch uses four Monte Carlo equity samples per decision. A separate 200-seed matched check in each mode uses 12 samples. A 500-seed matched first-orbit experiment in each mode changes starting chips from 200 to 400 at four samples. After discovering the sample-budget sensitivity, another 100 seeds per mode were run at the app default of 24 samples, with matching 400-chip controls. Basic stack controls end after the first orbit. The same seeds couple experiments, but decisions and later deals may diverge. No game rules or bot policies were modified for this study. The workspace gained an optional continuous-orbits setting during execution; a separately recovered, hash-verified initial source snapshot pins every batch to the same rules. Three riichi seed records reproduced byte-for-byte against that snapshot. These basic results describe four reset games, not four continuous orbits with one bankroll.\n')
add('The following large-batch tables use four samples unless explicitly labeled otherwise.\n')
table(['Measurement','Basic tournaments','Riichi games'],[
 ['Runs',n(b['runs']),n(r['runs'])],['Played hands',n(b['hands']),n(r['hands'])],['Showdown hands',pct(b['showdownHands']/b['hands']),pct(r['showdownHands']/r['hands'])],['Hands involving an all-in',pct(b['allInHandRate']),pct(r['allInHandRate'])],['Reach Street 4',pct(b['endingStreets'].get('4',0)/b['hands']),pct(r['endingStreets'].get('4',0)/r['hands'])],['Mean / 90th-percentile pot',f(b['pot']['mean'])+' / '+f(b['pot']['p90']),f(r['pot']['mean'])+' / '+f(r['pot']['p90'])],['Accounting violations',n(len(b['violations'])),n(len(r['violations']))]])
add('Across all 5,800 runs, 50,162 hands and 1,765,316 automated steps completed. Chip conservation and finite/nonnegative stacks were checked after every automated step. Final payouts, stick supply, orbit completion, aggregate scores, and the 50-chip net score cost per loan were checked separately. At startup, all 70 existing tests passed. Project TypeScript checking at that time encountered a pre-existing `scripts/analyze-ladder.ts:22` error; the new runner passed its focused type/lint checks. Zero observed violations is evidence for these checks, not a proof that all rules are bug-free.\n')
add('## Basic eliminations and chip adequacy\n')
